WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.428 --> 00:00:19.092
"You Ello cried as the inflatable boat bumped against the houseboat.

2
00:00:19.712 --> 00:00:20.713
"I thought you wouldn't!"

3
00:00:20.733 --> 00:00:23.413
"Of course we came," Zann said.

4
00:00:24.054 --> 00:00:26.914
He was happy to finally see Ello's face in person.

5
00:00:27.795 --> 00:00:28.335
"Help us up."

6
00:00:28.955 --> 00:00:30.135
Ello held out his hand.

7
00:00:30.715 --> 00:00:36.486
Everyone climbed up onto the houseboat's deck, and then Zann and Darb pulled up the inflatable boat.

8
00:00:37.607 --> 00:00:39.448
Gliss turned to smile at Ello.

9
00:00:39.468 --> 00:00:41.509
"We're glad you're safe!"

10
00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:43.951
she cried, flinging her arms around him.

11
00:00:43.971 --> 00:00:48.014
"Hey!" Ello shook off her hug and took a quick step back.

12
00:00:48.674 --> 00:00:49.655
Perda frowned at him.

13
00:00:49.675 --> 00:00:50.655
"What's wrong?"

14
00:00:51.556 --> 00:00:53.117
"Nothing," Ello said quickly.

15
00:00:53.137 --> 00:00:55.098
"Uh, I'm sorry.

16
00:00:55.599 --> 00:00:57.060
I've been alone so long.

17
00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:59.882
I guess I've forgotten how to act around people."

18
00:01:01.022 --> 00:01:02.223
Zann glanced around.

19
00:01:02.243 --> 00:01:05.917
"Wow, this houseboat is bigger than it looked from a distance."

20
00:01:06.617 --> 00:01:09.538
He bent to peer at an odd stain on the floor.

21
00:01:10.238 --> 00:01:12.839
The boat was missing a few chunks of wood here and there too.

22
00:01:13.699 --> 00:01:15.959
But for the most part, the vessel seemed sturdy.

23
00:01:15.979 --> 00:01:18.080
"Why are you alone?"

24
00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:19.400
Gliss asked Ello.

25
00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:21.221
"What happened to your people?"

26
00:01:21.901 --> 00:01:23.021
Ello scratched his head.

27
00:01:23.602 --> 00:01:25.522
He was wearing a pair of dark gloves.

28
00:01:26.142 --> 00:01:29.543
That seemed a little odd to Zann, but he soon forgot about it.

29
00:01:30.163 --> 00:01:32.104
There were more important questions to be answered.

30
00:01:33.436 --> 00:01:36.598
"Wyssa said she was going to come back and rescue you," Zann said.

31
00:01:36.618 --> 00:01:37.959
"Didn't she do that?"

32
00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:39.500
Ello frowned.

33
00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:41.302
"She did come back to Skellia.

34
00:01:41.962 --> 00:01:47.926
She promised to take all of them—uh, I mean us—to an unoccupied world where we could resettle.

35
00:01:48.487 --> 00:01:51.208
But when they left, I was at the back of the group.

36
00:01:51.669 --> 00:01:53.330
They accidentally left me behind."

37
00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:55.211
Gliss gasped.

38
00:01:55.231 --> 00:01:56.912
"That's horrible!

39
00:01:57.613 --> 00:01:59.174
Didn't she come back for you?"

40
00:02:00.255 --> 00:02:01.756
Zann was wondering the same thing.

41
00:02:02.452 --> 00:02:07.494
Wyssa might be kind of cranky and unpredictable, but she had very strong magical powers.

42
00:02:08.735 --> 00:02:12.796
She could have easily come back and rescued Ello once she realized he was missing.

43
00:02:12.816 --> 00:02:14.477
"Obviously not."

44
00:02:14.877 --> 00:02:17.078
Ello frowned, looking around the houseboat.

45
00:02:17.098 --> 00:02:21.020
"I figured a gulper must have eaten all the wormholes after they left.

46
00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:23.961
Or maybe she just didn't bother to come back for me."

47
00:02:24.661 --> 00:02:25.162
He shrugged.

48
00:02:25.182 --> 00:02:28.463
"Wyssa probably had other things on her mind besides helping me."

49
00:02:29.623 --> 00:02:30.664
Ello sounded bitter.

50
00:02:31.452 --> 00:02:32.553
Zann was surprised.

51
00:02:33.273 --> 00:02:39.656
The last time Zann had met Ello, the Skellian boy was kind and optimistic despite his people's dire

52
00:02:39.676 --> 00:02:43.477
situation. But Ello had been alone for a long time now.

53
00:02:44.358 --> 00:02:47.039
He'd been left behind and apparently forgotten.

54
00:02:47.739 --> 00:02:49.960
Anyone in his situation would be bitter.

55
00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:54.342
Darb was peering through a door leading to the interior of the houseboat.

56
00:02:55.322 --> 00:02:57.243
"This place is pretty nice," he said.

57
00:02:57.263 --> 00:02:58.984
"Where did it come from?"

58
00:03:00.012 --> 00:03:01.053
"Where did what come from?"

59
00:03:01.373 --> 00:03:05.635
Ello fiddled with the tips of one glove, not looking at Zann or his friends.

60
00:03:05.655 --> 00:03:08.137
"The houseboat," Perda said.

61
00:03:08.777 --> 00:03:09.938
She sounded impatient.

62
00:03:10.318 --> 00:03:12.099
"Where did you get this houseboat?"

63
00:03:12.119 --> 00:03:14.740
"I made it, of course," Ello said.

64
00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:18.262
"Really?" Darb stared at him in surprise.

65
00:03:19.003 --> 00:03:22.505
Zann and the girls walked over to Darb and looked through the door too.

66
00:03:23.205 --> 00:03:27.828
The interior room contained a bed, a table, and various other necessities.

67
00:03:28.672 --> 00:03:31.873
"But your people don't have much magic," Gliss blurted out.

68
00:03:31.893 --> 00:03:35.215
"How in the world did you make all this stuff?"

69
00:03:36.375 --> 00:03:37.636
"Yeah," Zann said.

70
00:03:37.656 --> 00:03:39.137
"Uh, no offense.

71
00:03:39.517 --> 00:03:43.238
But last time we met, you could barely conjure food or water.

72
00:03:43.899 --> 00:03:46.700
So how did you manage to conjure this boat all by yourself?"

73
00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:50.142
Ello looked away from them and bit his lip.

74
00:03:50.162 --> 00:03:53.303
"Um I'll tell you about it later, okay?

75
00:03:53.963 --> 00:03:55.484
Right now we have to get out of here.

76
00:03:56.148 --> 00:03:59.250
A storm is coming, and my boat just sprang a leak this morning.

77
00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:03.313
See?" He knelt down and placed his gloved palm on the deck.

78
00:04:03.994 --> 00:04:08.157
At that moment Zann was distracted by the guidelink, which jumped in his pocket.

79
00:04:08.717 --> 00:04:10.959
He glanced down and wondered what had set it off.

80
00:04:11.819 --> 00:04:13.981
Then he noticed a gulper glide by.

81
00:04:14.601 --> 00:04:17.683
Perhaps that creature's magic had caused the guidelink to jump?

82
00:04:18.244 --> 00:04:19.945
He turned his attention back to Ello.

83
00:04:20.645 --> 00:04:22.447
Ello had just stood up again.

84
00:04:23.107 --> 00:04:27.422
In the spot he'd touched, water was welling up through a crack in the boards.

85
00:04:28.242 --> 00:04:30.383
"Yikes!" Perda stared at the leak.

86
00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:32.544
"I didn't see that at first.

87
00:04:33.425 --> 00:04:35.526
You're right—we need to get out of here."

88
00:04:35.546 --> 00:04:39.648
"Especially if Ello’s correct and there's going to be a storm."

89
00:04:40.348 --> 00:04:41.969
Darb squinted up at the sky.

90
00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:43.670
Zann looked up too.

91
00:04:44.491 --> 00:04:50.534
As usual on Skellia, the sky was filled with foreboding clouds, though the sun was peeking through in

92
00:04:50.554 --> 00:04:51.234
a few spots.

93
00:04:52.015 --> 00:04:54.828
It didn't look particularly stormy to Zann.

94
00:04:54.848 --> 00:04:58.471
But he assumed Ello knew the weather on Skellia much better than he did.

95
00:04:58.491 --> 00:05:00.932
"Okay, let's take our boat," he said.

96
00:05:00.952 --> 00:05:03.534
"We can use the guidelink to find a wormhole."

97
00:05:04.355 --> 00:05:04.995
"The what?"

98
00:05:05.295 --> 00:05:06.576
Ello sounded curious.

99
00:05:07.617 --> 00:05:12.940
While Darb and the girls tossed the boat back into the sea, Zann quickly told Ello about the

100
00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:16.623
guidelink. "Its power will attract gulpers," Zann said.

101
00:05:16.643 --> 00:05:20.145
"But if we're quick, we can get through a wormhole before they catch up."

102
00:05:20.866 --> 00:05:23.708
By then the other three kids were already in the boat.

103
00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:25.041
"Hurry up!"

104
00:05:25.341 --> 00:05:25.901
Perda called.

105
00:05:25.921 --> 00:05:29.023
"Coming!" Zann jumped into the smaller boat.

106
00:05:29.743 --> 00:05:30.764
Then he looked up.

107
00:05:30.784 --> 00:05:31.684
"Come on, Ello!"

108
00:05:32.625 --> 00:05:35.967
Ello hesitated, looking fearful as he stared down at them.

109
00:05:36.727 --> 00:05:38.108
"Hurry!" Gliss cried.

110
00:05:38.828 --> 00:05:40.889
Finally Ello jumped off the deck.

111
00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:44.912
Just then a large wave pushed the small boat away.

112
00:05:45.592 --> 00:05:50.155
Ello let out a cry as he plunged into the sea between the two vessels.

113
00:05:50.175 --> 00:05:52.456
"Oops," Zann said.

114
00:05:52.824 --> 00:05:54.686
"Get ready to help him aboard when he surfaces."

115
00:05:55.847 --> 00:05:58.710
He leaned over the side, ready to grab Ello's hand.

116
00:05:59.651 --> 00:06:03.395
But when Ello's head finally popped into view, he was too far away.

117
00:06:03.415 --> 00:06:05.417
"Swim this way!"

118
00:06:05.778 --> 00:06:06.379
Perda called.

119
00:06:07.159 --> 00:06:08.481
Ello's arms flailed.

120
00:06:09.382 --> 00:06:11.664
He gurgled and sank underwater again.

121
00:06:11.684 --> 00:06:13.186
"Oh no!"

122
00:06:13.426 --> 00:06:14.047
Gliss cried.

123
00:06:14.067 --> 00:06:15.348
"I think he's drowning!"
